  "body": "Is it possible to add an attribute or property called **cache** with a default value of **true**? If disabled, it works like a cache busting token that gets the file's size in B, kB, KiB, KB or whatever is more precise and then appends that size as a query string. \r\n\r\nIf cache busting is intended, I doubt a single character change would have the same file size (or I could be wrong).\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n`<script src=\"app.js\" cache=\"false\"></script>`\r\n\r\nWhich will automatically then be rendered by browsers to something like:\r\n`<script src=\"app.js?filesize=123\"></script>`\r\n\r\nThe same goes for the `<link>` tag.",
